        "choice",
        "beginnings",
        "one-liner"
      ],
      "addedAt": "2026-07-05T03:48:30Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "scifi-044",
      "content": "Choice is an illusion, created between those with power, and those without.",
      "authorName": "The Merovingian (Lambert Wilson)",
      "source": "The Matrix Reloaded (2003)",
      "sourceType": "movie",
      "quoteDate": "2003-05-15",
      "verificationStatus": "verified",
      "notes": "The Merovingian's determinist counter-argument to Morpheus at Le Vrai restaurant.",
      "tags": [
        "choice",
        "power",
        "paradox"
      ],
      "addedAt": "2026-07-05T03:48:30Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "scifi-045",
      "content": "Everything that has a beginning has an end, Neo.",
      "authorName": "Agent Smith (Hugo Weaving)",
      "source": "The Matrix Revolutions (2003)",
      "sourceType": "movie",
      "quoteDate": "2003-11-05",
      "verificationStatus": "verified",
      "notes": "Smith recalling the Oracle's words during the climactic rain-soaked duel with Neo.",
      "tags": [
        "endings",
        "impermanence",
        "one-liner"
      ],
      "addedAt": "2026-07-05T03:48:30Z"
    },
    {
